{% comment %}
  Renders the "pick your free perfume" block for the cart — one slot per
  qualifying perfume unit in the cart (buy 3, pick 3 free perfumes
  independently).

  As of 2026-08-29 the gift is a small-size **perfume bottle** drawn from the
  signature-series collection itself, not a roll-on — Burhan asked for the
  roll-on gift to be replaced with this. The gift collection and the
  qualifying collection are now the same collection by default (both default
  to `signature-series`), which is different from the old roll-on setup where
  they were always two disjoint collections. See the "exact match, not
  contains" and "gift-size safeguard" notes below — both exist specifically
  because gift and qualifying products can now be the same product.

  How it works:
  - The customer earns one slot per unit of a qualifying-collection product in
    the cart (default: signature-series, i.e. the full-size perfumes). 2
    perfumes = 2 slots, each pickable independently.
  - The gift size a slot can be filled with depends on the bottle size that
    earned it: a 50ml bottle earns a slot fillable only with a 10ml perfume; a
    100ml bottle (or any size that isn't recognised as 50ml — covers every
    perfume sold before the 50ml option existed) earns a slot fillable only
    with a 35ml perfume. The two pools are tracked and rendered separately so
    a mixed-size cart can't spend one size's earned slot on the other size's
    gift.
  - Every match against a variant's Size option (option1) is an **exact**
    equality check (`== '10ML'`), never `contains`. `contains '10'` was safe
    back when the gift pool was roll-ons (whose only sizes are 6/12/10/35ml),
    but the gift pool is now the same perfumes that also come in 100ML — and
    "100ML" contains the substring "10". A `contains` check here would treat a
    customer's own full-price 100ml bottle as if it were the 10ml gift
    variant. Don't reintroduce `contains` on this option.
  - Each claimed slot is an ordinary cart line carrying the properties `Gift`
    (visible, so it shows on the order) and `_free_gift` (hidden marker this
    snippet and free-gift.js look for). Picking the same perfume for two slots
    just raises that line's quantity — each unit still fills exactly one slot.
  - Once claimed, a slot shows the chosen perfume and its price; that price
    only reads ₹0 when the discount function is actually doing its job.
  - The **offer discount function** (the same automatic discount that prices the
    bundles) is what makes claimed slots free — it zeroes up to one unit per
    earned slot across every line marked `_free_gift`. This snippet never fakes
    the price: the "Free" badge only appears once a slot actually costs
    nothing, so a missing discount is visible instead of silent. The function
    also re-checks that the line's own variant is genuinely a 10ml/35ml size
    (not just that the product is in the qualifying collection) — necessary
    now that gift and qualifying collection are the same, see the function's
    own comments.
  - "Change" on a claimed slot only removes that one unit, freeing the slot —
    it reappears as a picker row on the next render.

  Settings live in the theme customizer under Theme settings → Free gift, so the
  cart page and the cart drawer stay in sync from one place.

  Accepts:
  - context {String} 'page' or 'drawer' — only used to keep element ids unique

  Usage:
  {% render 'free-gift-picker', context: 'page' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign gift_collection = settings.free_gift_collection
  if gift_collection == blank
    assign gift_collection = collections['signature-series']
  endif

  assign qualifying_collection = settings.free_gift_qualifying_collection
  if qualifying_collection == blank
    assign qualifying_collection = collections['signature-series']
  endif

  # Two separate pools, keyed by the bottle size that earns them: '50' for a
  # 50ml bottle (fillable with a 10ml gift perfume), '100' for everything else
  # (fillable with a 35ml gift perfume — also the safe default for any perfume
  # variant title this doesn't recognise). claimed_* may briefly exceed
  # qualifying_* if the customer bumps a qualifying item's quantity down
  # after claiming — free-gift.js trims the excess, per pool, on load.
  assign qualifying_50 = 0
  assign qualifying_100 = 0
  assign claimed_50 = 0
  assign claimed_100 = 0
  assign bogus_gift_line_keys = ''

  for item in cart.items
    if item.properties._free_gift != blank
      if item.variant.option1 == '10ML'
        assign claimed_50 = claimed_50 | plus: item.quantity
      else
        assign claimed_100 = claimed_100 | plus: item.quantity
      endif
      continue
    endif

    assign in_qualifying_collection = false
    for c in item.product.collections
      if c.handle == qualifying_collection.handle
        assign in_qualifying_collection = true
        break
      endif
    endfor

    # Customize Perfume isn't in (and shouldn't be added to) the
    # signature-series collection — it's a different product entirely — but
    # Burhan wants a purchase of it to earn a free gift the same way a
    # signature-series perfume does. Handle-based, not collection-based, so
    # this one exception doesn't pull it into signature-series merchandising
    # or the price/variant-picker logic scoped to that collection elsewhere.
    # Attar roll-ons are deliberately not included — they live in their own
    # `attar-roll-ons` collection, untouched by this check either way.
    if item.product.handle == 'customize-perfume-1'
      assign in_qualifying_collection = true
    endif

    if in_qualifying_collection
      if item.variant.option1 == '10ML' or item.variant.option1 == '35ML'
        # A 10ml/35ml line with no `_free_gift` marker is the gift-only
        # placeholder-priced variant added directly (not through the gift
        # pickers) — it must never count as a real qualifying purchase (that
        # would silently hand out an extra free gift slot it didn't earn),
        # and it must never be treated as an ordinarily sellable line either.
        # Flagged here and force-removed by free-gift.js / blocked at
        # checkout as a hard backstop — see sections/main-cart-footer.liquid.
        assign bogus_gift_line_keys = bogus_gift_line_keys | append: item.key | append: ','
      elsif item.variant.option1 == '50ML'
        assign qualifying_50 = qualifying_50 | plus: item.quantity
      else
        assign qualifying_100 = qualifying_100 | plus: item.quantity
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign qualifying_units = qualifying_50 | plus: qualifying_100
  assign claimed_units = claimed_50 | plus: claimed_100

  assign qualifies = false
  if qualifying_units > 0
    assign qualifies = true
  endif

  # Only show this block once the cart actually qualifies (or already holds a
  # claimed gift line that still needs to render so it stays trimmable — see
  # the claimed-rows comment below). A cart holding only non-qualifying items
  # (e.g. attar roll-ons only) gets no "unlock a free perfume" nudge at all —
  # reported by Burhan 2026-08-31: the box was showing on an attar-only cart,
  # which can never qualify (roll-ons aren't in the qualifying collection),
  # so the nudge was pure clutter with nothing for the customer to do about it.
  assign show_block = false
  if settings.free_gift_enabled and gift_collection.products_count > 0
    if qualifies or claimed_units > 0
      assign show_block = true
    endif
  endif

  # A bogus (bare, non-`_free_gift`) 10ml/35ml line must render this block
  # regardless of the above — it's the only place free-gift.js's cleanup can
  # find it and force it out of the cart, and the only place checkout gets
  # blocked while it's still there. Independent of settings.free_gift_enabled:
  # these placeholder-priced sizes must never be sellable even if the whole
  # gift feature is switched off.
  if bogus_gift_line_keys != ''
    assign show_block = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_block -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign remaining_50 = qualifying_50 | minus: claimed_50
    if remaining_50 < 0
      assign remaining_50 = 0
    endif

    assign remaining_100 = qualifying_100 | minus: claimed_100
    if remaining_100 < 0
      assign remaining_100 = 0
    endif

    assign remaining_slots = remaining_50 | plus: remaining_100

    assign has_priced_slot = false
  -%}

  <free-gift-picker
    class="free-gift{% if claimed_units > 0 %} free-gift--claimed{% endif %}"
    id="FreeGift-{{ context | default: 'page' }}"
    data-context="{{ context | default: 'page' }}"
    data-qualifies="{{ qualifies }}"
    {%- comment -%}
      Named "-ten"/"-thirtyfive", not "-50"/"-100": a data-* attribute name
      with a hyphen immediately followed by a digit does NOT camelCase per
      the HTML spec (only hyphen+lowercase-letter converts), so
      data-qualifying-50 would silently read back as undefined via
      dataset.qualifying50 — the exact bug that made the excess-trim below
      compute 0 no matter what the cart actually held. Same landmine already
      documented for product-gift-picker.js's data-gift-variant-small/large.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    data-qualifying-ten="{{ qualifying_50 }}"
    data-claimed-ten="{{ claimed_50 }}"
    data-qualifying-thirtyfive="{{ qualifying_100 }}"
    data-claimed-thirtyfive="{{ claimed_100 }}"
    data-bogus-gift-keys="{{ bogus_gift_line_keys | strip_newlines | strip }}"
    data-gift-label="{{ settings.free_gift_heading | default: 'Your free perfume' | escape }}"
    {%- comment -%}
      Rendered purely so free-gift.js can find and force-remove a bogus line
      when the cart otherwise has nothing qualifying or claimed — nothing
      user-facing belongs on screen in that case, just a "pick your free
      perfume" promo with no perfume in the cart to earn it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if qualifies == false and claimed_units == 0 %} hidden{% endif %}
  >
    <div class="free-gift__head">
      <span class="free-gift__icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon-discount' %}</span>
      <div class="free-gift__head-text">
        <p class="free-gift__heading">
          {{- settings.free_gift_heading | default: 'Your free perfume' -}}
          {%- if qualifying_units > 1 %} &times; {{ qualifying_units }}{% endif -%}
        </p>
        <p class="free-gift__subtext">
          {%- if qualifies == false -%}
            {{ settings.free_gift_locked_text | default: 'Add any perfume to unlock a free perfume.' }}
          {%- elsif remaining_slots == 0 -%}
            {{ settings.free_gift_subtext | default: 'Pick one on us — no code needed.' }}
          {%- else -%}
            Pick {{ remaining_slots }} more — on us, no code needed.
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Claimed rows render whenever a gift line exists, even if the cart no
      longer qualifies (`claimed_units > 0` alone, not `qualifies`) — this is
      what lets free-gift.js's trimExcess actually find and remove a gift
      whose qualifying perfume was since removed from the cart. Gating this
      on `qualifies` alone left an orphaned gift line invisible to the DOM
      (and therefore untrimmable) the moment qualifying_units hit 0: the
      claimed-rows loop never ran, so no data-gift-line-key existed for the
      JS to act on, and the gift line just sat there — reverted to full price
      by the discount function (it doesn't care about DOM state), but never
      auto-removed. Reported by Burhan 2026-08-30.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if qualifies or claimed_units > 0 -%}
      {%- for item in cart.items -%}
        {%- if item.properties._free_gift != blank -%}
          {%- if item.final_price == 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%} at least one slot is genuinely free — no warning needed {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign has_priced_slot = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if item.variant.option1 == '10ML' -%}
            {%- assign row_bucket = '50' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign row_bucket = '100' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for i in (1..item.quantity) -%}
            <div
              class="free-gift__claimed"
              data-free-gift-row
              data-gift-line-key="{{ item.key }}"
              data-gift-variant-id="{{ item.variant_id }}"
              data-line-quantity="{{ item.quantity }}"
              data-gift-bucket="{{ row_bucket }}"
            >
              <span class="free-gift__claimed-name">{{ item.product.title | escape }}</span>
              {%- if item.final_price == 0 -%}
                <span class="free-gift__claimed-tag">Free gift</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="free-gift__claimed-price">{{ item.final_price | money }}</span>
              <button type="button" class="free-gift__change" data-free-gift-change>
                {{- 'Change' -}}
              </button>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Merchant-only warning: a claimed slot is in the cart but still costs
        money, which means the offer discount function isn't doing its job.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.design_mode and has_priced_slot -%}
        <p class="free-gift__warning">
          A claimed gift is still being charged. Check that the offer discount is
          active in Admin &rarr; Discounts, and that the two collections chosen in
          Theme settings &rarr; Free gift are the ones the discount function knows
          about.
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if remaining_50 > 0 -%}
        {%- for i in (1..remaining_50) -%}
          <div class="free-gift__options" data-free-gift-row data-free-gift-empty data-gift-bucket="50">
            <p class="free-gift__slot-label">10ml perfume</p>
            <div class="free-gift__select-wrap">
              <select
                class="free-gift__select"
                data-free-gift-select
                aria-label="10ml {{ settings.free_gift_heading | default: 'Your free perfume' | escape }}"
              >
                <option value="" selected disabled>
                  {{- settings.free_gift_choose_label | default: 'Choose' -}} &hellip;
                </option>
                {%- liquid
                  # The configurable "Customize Perfume" must never be given
                  # away free — skip it no matter which collection it sits in. A
                  # separate counter keeps it from eating a slot in the 12-item cap.
                  assign gift_slot = 0
                -%}
                {%- for gift in gift_collection.products -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign gift_title_lower = gift.title | downcase
                    if gift_title_lower contains 'customize'
                      continue
                    endif
                  -%}
                  {%- assign gift_variant = blank -%}
                  {%- for v in gift.variants -%}
                    {%- if v.option1 == '10ML' -%}
                      {%- assign gift_variant = v -%}
                      {%- break -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if gift_variant == blank -%}
                    {%- continue -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign gift_slot = gift_slot | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- if gift_slot > 12 -%}
                    {%- break -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Not gated on gift_variant.available: these are giveaway
                    units, not stock the merchant intends to sell separately,
                    and inventory counts on a newly added size variant aren't
                    reliably kept in sync. A slot the customer has genuinely
                    earned should never be unselectable.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <option value="{{ gift_variant.id }}" data-title="{{ gift.title | escape }}">
                    {{- gift.title | escape -}}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if remaining_100 > 0 -%}
        {%- for i in (1..remaining_100) -%}
          <div class="free-gift__options" data-free-gift-row data-free-gift-empty data-gift-bucket="100">
            <p class="free-gift__slot-label">35ml perfume</p>
            <div class="free-gift__select-wrap">
              <select
                class="free-gift__select"
                data-free-gift-select
                aria-label="35ml {{ settings.free_gift_heading | default: 'Your free perfume' | escape }}"
              >
                <option value="" selected disabled>
                  {{- settings.free_gift_choose_label | default: 'Choose' -}} &hellip;
                </option>
                {%- liquid
                  assign gift_slot = 0
                -%}
                {%- for gift in gift_collection.products -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign gift_title_lower = gift.title | downcase
                    if gift_title_lower contains 'customize'
                      continue
                    endif
                  -%}
                  {%- assign gift_variant = blank -%}
                  {%- for v in gift.variants -%}
                    {%- if v.option1 == '35ML' -%}
                      {%- assign gift_variant = v -%}
                      {%- break -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if gift_variant == blank -%}
                    {%- continue -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign gift_slot = gift_slot | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- if gift_slot > 12 -%}
                    {%- break -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <option value="{{ gift_variant.id }}" data-title="{{ gift.title | escape }}">
                    {{- gift.title | escape -}}
                  </option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="free-gift__error" data-free-gift-error hidden role="alert"></p>
  </free-gift-picker>
{%- endif -%}
